From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-16
Subject: [PATCH jm-v7 002] panvk: allow Bifrost v6/v7 on kbase without PAN_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER biblioklept

Purpose: drop the PAN_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER gate for v6/v7 in
panvk_physical_device_init_kbase() only (the DRM path keeps it) and log a
warning that Bifrost support is experimental instead. Lets testers create a
device and get a PanProbe baseline. v9+ cases are unchanged.
Source/Reference: JimVulkan/mali-panvk (MIT, warns and continues on v6/v7)
Tested GPU: build-checked (universal Android build v6-v14); not run on a Bifrost device
Tested Kbase UAPI: none
Mesa base range: 5a07217f + g615-v11-csf series + jm-v9 001-030
Dependencies: jm-v7 001
Validation test: vkCreateDevice on a G52 MC2 / G76 (pending)

---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c | 9 ++-------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
index 6369027c27d..6a79a7308e9 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1389,13 +1389,8 @@ panvk_physical_device_init_kbase(struct panvk_physical_device *device,
    switch (arch) {
    case 6:
    case 7:
-      if (!os_get_option("PAN_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER")) {
-         result = panvk_errorf(instance, VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER,
-                               "WARNING: panvk is not well-tested on v%d, "
-                               "pass PAN_I_WANT_A_BROKEN_VULKAN_DRIVER=1 "
-                               "if you know what you're doing.", arch);
-         goto fail_kbase;
-      }
+      /* Bifrost over kbase JM (jm-v7 series): experimental, no gate. */
+      mesa_logw("panvk: v%u (Bifrost) support is experimental", arch);
       break;
 
    case 9: /* Valhall JM over kbase job atoms (jm-v9 series) */
